{#- drift_check: a minion-side Salt schedule runs `state.apply test=True`
   every interval_minutes (+ up to splay_seconds, so the minions don't all
   hit the master at once) and writes the outcome as node-exporter textfile
   metrics (salt_drift_*). Prometheus alerts on them (pillar/prometheus.sls).

   textfile_dir: Debian's prometheus-node-exporter reads this directory by
   default (no --collector.textfile.directory flag needed) — verified on all
   minions 2026-10-18. It belongs to the node-exporter package, hence the
   require on that formula.

   timeout_seconds: while another state run holds the lock the script
   retries every 30 s; the timeout caps that wait plus the run itself
   (arrstack's dry run takes ~25 s). With enforce it caps each of the
   dry run, the repair apply and the second dry run.

   enforce: self-repair — on drift, run a real state.apply instead of only
   reporting. Off by default; turned on per minion in pillar where a
   re-apply is harmless (pillar/salt-minion-enforce.sls).

   enforce_window: limits enforce to a daily time window ("HH:MM" start/end
   in `timezone`, may wrap midnight). Outside it the check only reports.
   Empty start/end = always (homepage, monitoring, salt-master). Must be
   wider than interval_minutes + splay or a night can pass without a run.
   For hosts where a repair is disruptive but fine while nobody watches
   (arrstack, jellyfin: pillar/salt-minion-enforce-window.sls).

   beacons.service: Salt's service beacon, persisted to
   /etc/salt/minion.d/beacons.conf. Fires salt/beacon/<id>/service/<name>
   only on a status change (onchangeonly), not at minion start
   (emitatstartup off). The master's reactor (formulas/salt-master) starts
   a stopped service again if it is on its whitelist. delay_seconds must
   exceed the unit's StartLimitIntervalSec (docker: 1 min): systemd's own
   Restart= gets the first go, and once it gave up (start limit hit) the
   reactor's `systemctl start` would be refused until that interval passed.
   Off by default; on per minion in pillar/salt-minion-beacons.sls. #}
{%- set defaults = {
    'drift_check': {
        'enabled': True,
        'enforce': False,
        'enforce_window': {'start': '', 'end': '', 'timezone': 'UTC'},
        'interval_minutes': 60,
        'splay_seconds': 300,
        'timeout_seconds': 900,
        'script': '/usr/local/sbin/salt-drift-check',
        'textfile_dir': '/var/lib/prometheus/node-exporter',
        'metrics_file': 'salt_drift.prom',
        'salt_call': '/usr/bin/salt-call',
        'python': '/usr/bin/python3',
    },
    'beacons': {
        'service': {
            'enabled': False,
            'services': [],
            'interval_seconds': 10,
            'delay_seconds': 90,
        },
    },
} %}
{%- set salt_minion = salt['pillar.get']('salt-minion:lookup', default=defaults, merge=True) %}
